    {
      "id": "RF-J3A-1",
      "status": "CLOSED",
      "assessment": "The implementation takes r1's permitted alternative: ReservedExecutionId has no private inherent constructor. Its only inherent functions are public read-only as_str and bytes. RequestIdentity retains only public draw and bytes. The registry constructs ReservedExecutionId directly only after a successful uniqueness insert, both for normal allocation and the existing feature-only injected reservation. The census assertion is now true, and no seventeenth group-F fixture is needed.",
      "locations": [
        {
          "path": "crates/platform/src/lib.rs",
          "line": 124
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/platform/src/lib.rs",
          "line": 180
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/platform/src/crash_barrier.rs",
          "line": 782
        }
      ],
      "proof": "An independent plain-surface probe has a compiling reserve_execution_id control and exactly one E0599 for ReservedExecutionId::reserved([0; 16]); the former E0624 private helper is absent, rather than newly exported."
    }
  ],
